<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador to buy back $250 mln Brady bonds - paper.</title>
<headline>Ecuador to buy back $250 mln Brady bonds - paper.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's government will buy back $250 million in Brady bonds Friday, a local newspaper reported.</p>
<p>El Comercio did not name any sources for the information, but said that the goverment plans to use funds from a recent $500 million Eurobonds issue in the buyback.</p>
<p>Ecuador used most of the Eurobond money to cover a $300 million bridging loan from the Chase Manhattan Bank, El Comercio said.</p>
<p>No government official was immediately available for comment on the report.</p>
<p>((--Quito Newsroom +5932 25-8433))</p>
